  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, poll fixed for 15 January 1931. Six were nominated for the six seats on 2 January, all outgoing members except Stanley Haggan (Northern Whig, 3 January 1931, p. 8), so all six were returned unopposed (Belfast Telegraph, 6 January 1931, p. 6: except for Bangor and Portrush, no urban election in Ulster was contested). The retiring members had been named in the Northern Whig of 1 January 1931, p. 6; one of them, F. Atkinson, was not nominated. Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of the Northern Whig, 3 January 1931, p. 8 (w8-review, Nov 2026): the six nominated, one for each seat, were John Graham, Stanley Haggan, Chas. M. Legg, Wm. M'Cullough, Thos. J. Patterson and David C. Thompson, all outgoing members except Mr. Haggan; Stanley Haggan replaces F. Atkinson, a retiring member who was not nominated (he had been taken from the list of retiring members of 1 January)."
